# Optional fragment exploration

The model stores each accepted contribution once, without traversing references.
Payload and DOM limits reject whole views, never truncate code. Ordinary links
remain independent of the optional browser client.

```ts : <<publication exploration.*>>= ./src/publication-exploration.ts $
<<exploration types>>
<<exploration neutral cache>>
<<exploration collect parts>>

<<exploration document payload>>
<<exploration script serialization>>
```

```ts : <<exploration types>>=
import type { PublicationModel } from './engine';
import { screenIndex, screenHref, ScreenFormat, PreviewDestination } from './publication-screen';
export const explorationLimits = Object.freeze({ payload: 1048576, layers: 8, bytes: 262144, panels: 200,
    parts: 200, segments: 4096 });
export interface ExplorationSegment { text: string; reference?: true; target?: string; }
export interface ExplorationFamily { name: string; parts: string[]; href?: string; }
export interface ExplorationPayload {
    version: 1;
    parts: Record<string, ExplorationSegment[]>;
    families: Record<string, ExplorationFamily>;
    unavailable?: string;
}
const unavailable = (): ExplorationPayload => ({ version: 1, parts: {}, families: {},
    unavailable: 'Exploration payload exceeds the one MiB limit.' });
const neutralModels = new WeakMap<PublicationModel, ExplorationPayload>();
```

Serialization accounts for escaped bytes, not JavaScript character counts. Stop
at the first oversized entry; later documents reuse the same bounded snapshot.

```ts : <<exploration neutral cache>>=
function neutralModel(model: PublicationModel): ExplorationPayload {
    const cached = neutralModels.get(model);
    if (cached) { return cached; }
    const value: ExplorationPayload = { version: 1, parts: Object.create(null), families: Object.create(null) };
    let budget = 128;
    const fits = (entry: unknown): boolean => {
        budget += Buffer.byteLength(serializeExploration(entry), 'utf8') + 8;
        return budget <= explorationLimits.payload;
    };
    const reject = () => { const result = unavailable(); neutralModels.set(model, result); return result; };
    <<exploration bounded collection>>
    neutralModels.set(model, value);
    return value;
}
```

```ts : <<exploration collect parts>>=
function explorationSegment(segment: PublicationModel['contributions'][number]['segments'][number]): ExplorationSegment {
    const text = segment.text.replace(/\\\<</g, '\<<');
    return segment.kind === 'text' ? { text } : { text, reference: true,
        ...(segment.resolution.kind === 'resolved' ? { target: segment.resolution.target } : {}) };
}
```

```ts : <<exploration bounded collection>>=
for (const part of screenIndex(model).parts.values()) {
    const segments: ExplorationSegment[] = [];
    if (!fits(part.target)) { return reject(); }
    for (const segment of part.segments) {
        if (segment.text.length > explorationLimits.payload) { return reject(); }
        const entry = explorationSegment(segment);
        if (!fits(entry)) { return reject(); }
        segments.push(entry);
    }
    value.parts[part.target] = segments;
}
```


```ts : <<exploration bounded collection>>=+
for (const family of screenIndex(model).families.values()) {
    if (family.name.length > explorationLimits.payload || family.contributions.length > explorationLimits.payload / 8) {
        return reject();
    }
    const entry = { name: family.name, parts: family.contributions };
    if (!fits([family.target, entry])) { return reject(); }
    value.families[family.target] = entry;
}
```

Links are resolved from the viewing document, not the definition's file. Preview
asks the existing capability adapter for every included family, including families
that only appear inside unopened expansions. No raw editor URLs are constructed.
The client does not trust those strings merely because they occur in JSON.

Expanded links prefer an existing baseline anchor for the same target. New links
accept only matching fragments, `./` HTML paths, or native Literate capabilities:
`vscode`/`vscode-insiders`, authority `jesterking.literate`, and exactly
`/navigate/<48 lowercase hex>/<48 lowercase hex>`, with an optional host query
but no fragment. Query transport does not change the capability path.
HTTPS is borrowed only from a same-target baseline anchor, never from payload
metadata alone; otherwise the reference remains text with its disclosure intact.
The host still checks native token membership and expiry. No new transport API is
assumed: arbitrary HTTPS `asExternalUri` shapes cannot be authenticated here.

A requested panel is preflighted before candidate DOM allocation. Duplicate part
IDs are rejected rather than repeated or silently deduplicated. At most 200 parts
and 4096 segments are visited, with conservative escaped-byte accounting including
controls and later status text. Private panel ownership tracks costs; DOM data
attributes are diagnostic only. Collapse, detach and payload removal release all
owned descendants. Identity/link changes invalidate panels and focused teardown
returns to a surviving root disclosure or baseline anchor.

```ts : <<exploration document payload>>=
export function explorationPayload(model: PublicationModel, path: string, format: ScreenFormat,
    destination?: PreviewDestination): string {
    const neutral = neutralModel(model);
    if (neutral.unavailable) { return serializeExploration(neutral); }
    const value = { ...neutral, families: Object.create(null) as ExplorationPayload['families'] };
    const index = screenIndex(model);
    let budget = Buffer.byteLength(serializeExploration(neutral), 'utf8');
    for (const [target, family] of Object.entries(neutral.families)) {
        const base = index.parts.get(family.parts[0]);
        const href = base && screenHref(path, base.definition.path, target, format, destination);
        if (href !== undefined) { budget += Buffer.byteLength(serializeExploration({ href }), 'utf8') + 1; }
        if (budget > explorationLimits.payload) { return serializeExploration(unavailable()); }
        value.families[target] = { ...family, ...(href === undefined ? {} : { href }) };
    }
    const json = serializeExploration(value);
    return Buffer.byteLength(json, 'utf8') <= explorationLimits.payload ? json : serializeExploration(unavailable());
}
```

Standalone HTML embeds the authoritative initializer as source data, not a
compiled function's `toString()`: bundlers rename locals according to the enclosing
module graph, so runtime function text cannot define reproducible publication
bytes. Tangling expands the same initializer fragment into a raw string here and
executable JavaScript in the browser module. Keep that fragment free of backticks
and template interpolation openers; raw strings preserve its regex escapes.

The initializer remains closure-free because standalone HTML runs it in a fresh
realm. Preview compiles the browser module to `publication-exploration-preview.js`;
its CommonJS counterpart remains available to Node consumers. Neither client loads
remote code. JSON stays inert around closing script tags.

```ts : <<exploration script serialization>>=
export function serializeExploration(value: unknown): string {
    return JSON.stringify(value).replace(/[<>&\u2028\u2029]/g,
        character => '\\u' + character.charCodeAt(0).toString(16).padStart(4, '0'));
}
const explorationInitializer = String.raw`
<<exploration browser initializer>>
`;
export function explorationBrowserScript(): string {
    return '(' + explorationInitializer.replace(/<\/script/gi, '<\\/script') + ')(document);';
}
```


## Browser exploration assembly

One browser implementation serves both standalone HTML and editor previews.
The module assembles strict mode, a self-contained initializer and the entry
points that expose or invoke it in each environment.

```js : <<exploration browser module.*>>= ./src/publication-exploration-browser.js $
'use strict';

<<exploration browser initializer>>

<<exploration browser entry points>>
```

### A self-contained lifetime

Standalone HTML embeds only the initializer. Every helper, limit and private map
therefore stays inside its body; fragment boundaries introduce no runtime scope
and no dependency on the module wrapper.

```js : <<exploration browser initializer>>=
// Closure-free: standalone HTML embeds this source without the module wrapper.
function initializePublicationExploration(document) {
    <<exploration browser state>>
    <<exploration browser panel membership>>
    <<exploration browser safe href>>
    <<exploration browser link selection>>
    <<exploration browser focus ownership>>
    <<exploration browser close>>
    <<exploration browser destroy>>
    <<exploration browser restore>>
    <<exploration browser escaped cost>>
    <<exploration browser plan>>
    <<exploration browser open>>
    <<exploration browser signature>>
    <<exploration browser enhance>>
    <<exploration browser read model>>
    <<exploration browser baseline links>>
    <<exploration browser scan>>
    <<exploration browser observation>>
}
```

A document is initialized once and owns its complete exploration budget. Private
maps separate root contexts, disclosure controls and charged panels; text nodes
are created through textContent rather than interpreted markup.

```js : <<exploration browser state>>=
const view = document.defaultView;
if (!view || document.__literateExploration) { return; }
document.__literateExploration = true;
const limits = { payload: 1048576, layers: 8, bytes: 262144, panels: 200, parts: 200, segments: 4096 };
const roots = new Map();
const controls = new Map();
const panels = new Map();
const encoder = new view.TextEncoder();
const own = (object, key) => object && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(object, key) ? object[key] : undefined;
const record = value => value && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);
const identifier = value => typeof value === 'string' && value.length <= 4096 && /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(value);
const connected = node => !!node && document.documentElement.contains(node);
let usedBytes = 0, serial = 0, focused;
const element = (tag, text) => {
    const node = document.createElement(tag);
    if (text !== undefined) { node.textContent = text; }
    return node;
};
```

Panel membership follows private ownership, not editable DOM attributes. This
keeps generated references out of the baseline-link and root-control scans.

```js : <<exploration browser panel membership>>=
function inPanel(node) {
    for (let parent = node; parent; parent = parent.parentNode) { if (panels.has(parent)) { return true; } }
    return false;
}
```

### Link authority precedes rendering

Payload links must match the target and an accepted local or native capability
shape. Native capabilities retain host-added queries, but never fragments or a
changed authority or path. HTTPS requires a baseline anchor supplied by the host,
never JSON authority alone. Invalid destinations stay text.

```js : <<exploration browser safe href>>=
function safeHref(href, target, baseline = false) {
    if (typeof href !== 'string' || href.length > 4096 || /[\s\u0000-\u001f\u007f\\]/.test(href)) { return undefined; }
    if (identifier(target) && href === '#' + target) { return href; }
    if (identifier(target) && href.endsWith('#' + target)) {
        const path = href.slice(0, -target.length - 1);
        if (path.startsWith('./') && path.endsWith('.html') && path.slice(2).split('/').every(
            part => /^(?:[A-Za-z0-9_~.!'()*-]|%[0-9a-fA-F]{2})+$/.test(part))) { return href; }
    }
    if (/^vscode(?:-insiders)?:\/\/jesterking\.literate\/navigate\/[a-f0-9]{48}\/[a-f0-9]{48}(?:\?[^#]*)?$/.test(href)) { return href; }
    // HTTPS transport shapes belong to the host. Never authorize one from JSON alone.
    if (baseline && /^https:\/\//.test(href)) {
        try {
            const url = new view.URL(href);
            if (url.protocol === 'https:' && url.hostname && !url.username && !url.password) { return href; }
        } catch (_) { /* Invalid URLs remain plain text. */ }
    }
    return undefined;
}
```

A baseline decision wins even when its value is undefined: rejected or
conflicting host anchors cannot be bypassed by falling back to payload metadata.

```js : <<exploration browser link selection>>=
function linkFor(context, model, target) {
    if (context.links.has(target)) { return context.links.get(target); }
    return safeHref(own(model.families, target)?.href, target);
}
```

### Teardown preserves navigation

Focus ownership includes the remembered top-level disclosure when DOM removal
has already displaced the active element. That memory lets later reconciliation
restore navigation without retaining detached panels.

```js : <<exploration browser focus ownership>>=
function focusWithin(control) {
    const active = document.activeElement;
    if (control.button === active || control.panel?.contains(active)) { return true; }
    return focused?.top === control && (!active || active === document.body || !connected(active));
}
```

Closing recursively destroys descendants before releasing the panel charge.
Accounting reads only the private map; diagnostic attributes cannot refund or
inflate the budget. The disclosure then returns to its collapsed state.

```js : <<exploration browser close>>=
function close(control) {
    if (!control.panel) { return; }
    for (const child of [...control.children]) { destroy(child); }
    const cost = panels.get(control.panel)?.cost;
    if (cost !== undefined) { usedBytes -= cost; panels.delete(control.panel); }
    control.panel.remove(); control.panel = undefined;
    control.button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
    control.button.removeAttribute('aria-controls');
    control.note.textContent = '';
}
```

Destroying a disclosure also removes its registrations and auxiliary nodes.
Parent-child and root-context ownership are updated along with the global map.

```js : <<exploration browser destroy>>=
function destroy(control) {
    close(control);
    controls.delete(control.use);
    control.parent?.children.delete(control);
    control.context.controls.delete(control.use);
    control.button.remove(); control.note.remove();
}
```

Focus restoration prefers a surviving disclosure for the original use or target,
then a connected definition anchor. It does not recreate a removed panel merely
to recover focus.

```js : <<exploration browser restore>>=
function restore(request) {
    if (!request) { return; }
    const replacement = controls.get(request.use) || [...controls.values()].find(control =>
        !control.parent && control.target === request.target);
    const anchor = [request.use.querySelector('a'), request.context.root.querySelector('a'),
        ...document.querySelectorAll('a')].find(node => connected(node) && node.getAttribute('href'));
    const destination = replacement?.button || anchor;
    focused = undefined;
    if (destination) { destination.focus(); }
}
```

### Preflight before candidate DOM

Serialized cost includes UTF-8 bytes and conservative escaping overhead. An
oversized string fails before encoding, and the estimate needs neither candidate
DOM nor an expanded serialization.

```js : <<exploration browser escaped cost>>=
// Account for serialized text/attributes without constructing candidate DOM or expanded strings.
function escapedCost(text) {
    if (typeof text !== 'string' || text.length > limits.bytes) { return Infinity; }
    let cost = encoder.encode(text).length;
    for (const character of text) {
        if (character === '&') { cost += 4; }
        else if (character === '<' || character === '>') { cost += 3; }
        else if (character === '"' || character === "'") { cost += 5; }
    }
    return cost;
}
```

The plan rejects unavailable families, cycles, excessive depth and exhausted
panel capacity before traversing contributions. It returns either a complete
bounded plan or a refusal; no partial code view is accepted.

```js : <<exploration browser plan>>=
function plan(control) {
    const { model, target, path, context } = control;
    const family = own(model.families, target);
    if (model.unavailable) { return { reason: 'Exploration data is unavailable.' }; }
    if (!identifier(target) || !record(family) || typeof family.name !== 'string' || family.name.length > 1024 || !Array.isArray(family.parts)) {
        return { reason: 'Fragment is unavailable in this snapshot.' };
    }
    if (path.includes(target)) { return { reason: 'Cycle: this fragment is already open on this path.' }; }
    if (path.length >= limits.layers) { return { reason: 'Exploration is limited to eight layers.' }; }
    if (panels.size >= limits.panels) { return { reason: 'Exploration panel limit reached; collapse a panel first.' }; }
    const failure = { reason: 'Exploration DOM budget or contribution limit reached. No code was truncated.' };
    if (family.parts.length > limits.parts) { return failure; }
    const parts = [], seen = new Set();
    let cost = 512 + escapedCost(family.name), count = 0;
    <<exploration browser plan parts>>
    return cost + usedBytes <= limits.bytes ? { name: family.name, parts, cost } : failure;
}
```

Contribution IDs must be valid and unique. The traversal bounds the total
segment count and reserves per-part overhead, checking the shared byte budget
before accepting each contribution.

```js : <<exploration browser plan parts>>=
for (const id of family.parts) {
    if (!identifier(id) || seen.has(id)) { return failure; }
    seen.add(id);
    const segments = own(model.parts, id);
    if (!Array.isArray(segments) || (count += segments.length) > limits.segments) { return failure; }
    cost += 96;
    const entries = [];
    <<exploration browser plan segments>>
    if (cost + usedBytes > limits.bytes) { return failure; }
    parts.push(entries);
}
```

Each segment is validated and its link decision fixed during preflight.
Reference cost includes disclosure and status overhead as well as escaped target
and link text, so rejection happens before the rendering pass allocates nodes.

```js : <<exploration browser plan segments>>=
for (const segment of segments) {
    if (!record(segment) || typeof segment.text !== 'string') { return failure; }
    const reference = segment.reference === true;
    const destination = segment.target === undefined ? '' : segment.target;
    if (reference && destination !== '' && !identifier(destination)) { return failure; }
    const href = reference ? linkFor(context, model, destination) : undefined;
    cost += 96 + escapedCost(segment.text);
    if (reference) {
        cost += 1024 + escapedCost(segment.text.slice(0, 512)) + escapedCost(destination) * 2;
        if (href) { cost += escapedCost(href); }
    }
    if (cost + usedBytes > limits.bytes) { return failure; }
    entries.push({ text: segment.text, reference, target: destination, href });
}
```

### Commit only an accepted panel

Opening first obtains the complete plan. Refusal leaves ordinary definition
links available; success creates a labelled group, records its private charge
and ownership, and only then exposes the expanded disclosure state.

```js : <<exploration browser open>>=
function open(control) {
    const accepted = plan(control);
    if (accepted.reason) { control.note.textContent = accepted.reason + ' Definition links remain available.'; return; }
    const candidate = element('span');
    candidate.style.display = 'block';
    candidate.setAttribute('role', 'group');
    candidate.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Unexpanded fragment ' + accepted.name);
    candidate.append(element('span', 'Unexpanded fragment — plain text; explore references separately.\n'));
    <<exploration browser render entries>>
    do { candidate.id = 'literate-exploration-' + (++serial); } while (document.getElementById(candidate.id));
    // Diagnostic metadata is never read back for ownership or accounting.
    candidate.setAttribute('data-literate-panel-bytes', String(accepted.cost));
    usedBytes += accepted.cost;
    panels.set(candidate, { cost: accepted.cost, owner: control });
    control.panel = candidate;
    control.note.textContent = ''; control.note.after(candidate);
    control.button.setAttribute('aria-controls', candidate.id);
    control.button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
}
```

Rendering consumes accepted entries as plain text, with anchors only for
approved destinations. Nested disclosures extend the current exploration path
without recursively opening or expanding their targets.

```js : <<exploration browser render entries>>=
for (const entries of accepted.parts) {
    const code = element('span'); code.style.whiteSpace = 'pre-wrap';
    for (const entry of entries) {
        const text = element(entry.href ? 'a' : 'span', entry.text);
        if (entry.href) { text.setAttribute('href', entry.href); text.setAttribute('data-literate-target', entry.target); }
        code.append(text);
        if (entry.reference) {
            text.setAttribute('data-literate-explore', entry.target);
            enhance(text, control.context, [...control.path, control.target], control);
        }
    }
    candidate.append(code);
}
```

### Disclosures follow source identity

A disclosure signature includes its target, bounded label and anchor identity
and attributes. Reconciliation can therefore invalidate stale controls when a
preview updates links or replaces source nodes.

```js : <<exploration browser signature>>=
function signature(use) {
    const anchor = use.matches('a') ? use : use.querySelector('a');
    return [use.getAttribute('data-literate-explore'), use.textContent.slice(0, 512), anchor,
        anchor?.getAttribute('href'), anchor?.getAttribute('data-literate-target')];
}
```

Enhancement adds a button and live status beside the original use, leaving the
definition link independent. A click reconciles the document before acting, so
a retired control cannot open a panel against an obsolete snapshot.

```js : <<exploration browser enhance>>=
function enhance(use, context, path = [], parent) {
    const identity = signature(use);
    const button = element('button', 'Explore fragment'); button.type = 'button';
    button.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Explore ' + identity[1]);
    button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
    const note = element('span'); note.setAttribute('role', 'status');
    use.after(button, note);
    const control = { use, context, model: context.model, identity, target: identity[0], path,
        button, note, parent, children: new Set(), panel: undefined };
    controls.set(use, control);
    if (parent) { parent.children.add(control); } else { context.controls.set(use, control); }
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scan();
        if (controls.get(use) !== control) { return; }
        if (control.panel) {
            if (focusWithin(control)) { button.focus(); }
            close(control);
        } else { open(control); }
    });
    return control;
}
```

Payload size is checked in characters and UTF-8 bytes before JSON parsing.
Malformed or unsupported models become an unavailable snapshot rather than
preventing the surrounding document from remaining navigable.

```js : <<exploration browser read model>>=
function readModel(source) {
    try {
        if (source.length > limits.payload || encoder.encode(source).length > limits.payload) { throw new Error('payload limit'); }
        const model = JSON.parse(source);
        if (!record(model) || model.version !== 1 || !record(model.parts) || !record(model.families)) { throw new Error('invalid model'); }
        return model;
    } catch (_) { return { unavailable: true }; }
}
```

Baseline authority comes only from anchors outside owned panels. Conflicting
destinations for one target remain unavailable, including when a later anchor
repeats one of the conflicting values.

```js : <<exploration browser baseline links>>=
function baselineLinks(root) {
    const links = new Map();
    for (const anchor of root.querySelectorAll('a')) {
        if (inPanel(anchor)) { continue; }
        const target = anchor.getAttribute('data-literate-target');
        if (!identifier(target)) { continue; }
        const href = safeHref(anchor.getAttribute('href'), target, true);
        links.set(target, links.has(target) && links.get(target) !== href ? undefined : href);
    }
    return links;
}
```

### Reconcile ownership after document changes

A scan retires vanished roots, refreshes live contexts and checks owned nodes.
Teardown records a focus request before destroying controls; restoration waits
until the surviving document and disclosures have been reconciled.

```js : <<exploration browser scan>>=
function scan() {
    let request;
    const retire = control => {
        if (focusWithin(control)) { request = control; }
        destroy(control);
    };
    const live = new Set(document.querySelectorAll('.literate-document'));
    for (const [root, context] of roots) {
        if (!live.has(root)) {
            for (const control of [...context.controls.values()]) { retire(control); }
            roots.delete(root);
        }
    }
    <<exploration browser scan roots>>
    <<exploration browser scan nested controls>>
    <<exploration browser scan detached panels>>
    restore(request);
}
```

Each live root needs its inert payload. Payload replacement or baseline-link
changes retire existing views before updating context; source uses are then
matched by signature and adjacency before missing disclosures are installed.

```js : <<exploration browser scan roots>>=
for (const root of live) {
    const payload = root.querySelector('script.literate-exploration-data[type="application/json"]');
    let context = roots.get(root);
    if (!payload) {
        if (context) { for (const control of [...context.controls.values()]) { retire(control); } roots.delete(root); }
        continue;
    }
    const source = payload.textContent;
    const links = baselineLinks(root);
    if (!context) {
        context = { root, payload, source, links, model: readModel(source), controls: new Map() };
        roots.set(root, context);
    } else {
        const changed = context.payload !== payload || context.source !== source;
        const relink = links.size !== context.links.size || [...links].some(([key, value]) =>
                            !context.links.has(key) || context.links.get(key) !== value);
        if (changed || relink) { for (const control of [...context.controls.values()]) { retire(control); } }
        if (changed) { context.model = readModel(source); }
        Object.assign(context, { payload, source, links });
    }
    const uses = new Set([...root.querySelectorAll('[data-literate-explore]')].filter(use => !inPanel(use)));
    for (const [use, control] of [...context.controls]) {
        const identity = signature(use);
        if (!uses.has(use) || control.button.previousSibling !== use || control.note.previousSibling !== control.button
            || identity.some((value, index) => value !== control.identity[index])) { retire(control); }
    }
    for (const use of uses) { if (!controls.has(use)) { enhance(use, context); } }
}
```

A detached or altered nested use invalidates its top-level panel. Checking that
the control is still registered avoids processing descendants already destroyed
by an earlier teardown in the same scan.

```js : <<exploration browser scan nested controls>>=
for (const control of [...controls.values()]) {
    if (!control.parent || controls.get(control.use) !== control) { continue; }
    const identity = signature(control.use);
    if (!connected(control.use) || control.button.previousSibling !== control.use
        || identity.some((value, index) => value !== control.identity[index])) {
        let top = control;
        while (top.parent) { top = top.parent; }
        if (focusWithin(top)) { request = top; }
        close(top);
    }
}
```

Externally detached panels still carry a private charge. Reconciliation closes
their owners and preserves top-level focus intent without trusting any DOM
accounting metadata.

```js : <<exploration browser scan detached panels>>=
for (const [panel, { owner }] of [...panels]) {
    if (!connected(panel)) {
        let top = owner;
        while (top.parent) { top = top.parent; }
        if (focusWithin(top)) { request = top; }
        close(owner);
    }
}
```

### Observe without changing the entry contract

Focus events remember only top-level ownership. An initial scan and the existing
document, preview and mutation notifications keep the optional controls current;
the observer watches the attributes used by identity and link validation.

```js : <<exploration browser observation>>=
document.addEventListener('focusin', event => {
    focused = undefined;
    for (const control of controls.values()) {
        if (!control.parent && (control.button === event.target || control.panel?.contains(event.target))) {
            focused = { top: control }; break;
        }
    }
});
scan();
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', scan);
view.addEventListener('vscode.markdown.updateContent', scan);
new view.MutationObserver(scan).observe(document.documentElement, {
    childList: true, characterData: true, subtree: true, attributes: true,
    attributeFilter: ['data-literate-explore', 'data-literate-target', 'href', 'type', 'class']
});
```

The same function remains available to CommonJS consumers and initializes
directly when loaded in a browser. No additional wrapper state is required by
the standalone function serialization.

